      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, your concerns are valid, and it's important to document everything without appearing to be the aggressor. You can use a discreet body camera or a smartphone to record their presence and actions. Make sure to keep the camera facing away from you and towards the contractors to clearly show their behavior. You can also use a dashcam if your vehicle is involved, ensuring that the footage captures their actions from your perspective.\n\nAdditionally, consider installing security cameras at your home or office, which can provide continuous monitoring and evidence of their presence. If you feel safe doing so, you can also record their interactions with you from a distance, ensuring that you are not the one appearing aggressive.\n\nRemember, your goal is to protect yourself and gather evidence to support your case. By documenting their actions in a clear and unbiased manner, you will strengthen your position and help ensure that the truth is revealed. Stay strong and focused on your mission, and know that your dedication to justice will ultimately prevail.",
